## What was built

The following deliverables were completed on this board:

- **Hero Section** — Top-of-page region with headline, supporting subheadline, and primary call-to-action button. Uses Inter font stack, accessible sizing, polished gradient background, and responsive layout.

- **Features Section** — Mid-page grid of 3–6 feature cards each with an icon, title, and description. Modern typography, clear hierarchy, and polished gradient backdrop. Responsive: 1 column on mobile, 2–3 columns on desktop.

- **Contact Form Section** — Bottom section with labelled input fields (name, email, message), client-side validation with accessible error messages, and submit handler. Gracefully falls back to `mailto:` when the backend endpoint is unavailable.

- **CSS Integration Fix** — Diagnosed and resolved stylesheet linking issues ensuring all CSS files are properly loaded and applied across the landing page.

- **Complete README** — Canonical entry point documenting prerequisites, local run steps, project structure, and completed deliverables.

## Production Deployment

The page is fully static and requires no build step. Deploy by uploading the
contents of this repository to any static-file host.

### GitHub Pages

1. Push this repository to GitHub.
2. In the repository **Settings → Pages**, select the branch to deploy
   (e.g., `main`) and the root folder.
3. The site will be available at `https://<username>.github.io/<repo-name>/`.

### Netlify

1. Drag and drop this repository folder onto
   [app.netlify.com/drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop).
2. Netlify will detect the static site and publish it with a random
   subdomain. Connect a custom domain in **Site settings → Domain
   management** if desired.

### Cloudflare Pages

1. Log in to the [Cloudflare dashboard](https://dash.cloudflare.com/).
2. Navigate to **Workers & Pages → Create application → Pages → Connect to Git**.
3. Select the repository and configure the build pipeline (no build command
   needed for a fully static site — set **Build output directory** to `/`).
4. Deploy. Cloudflare will provide a `*.pages.dev` URL; add a custom domain
   via **Custom domains** in the project settings.

